course: dictionary
lesson: 11252
title: Worshipper: praying people and playful fans
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A worshipper is a person who worships. To worship means to pray to God or a god, and to praise them with love and respect. A worshipper is one of the people doing that.
explain: In stories about religion, worshippers fill a church, kneel, sing and pray together. The same word can also be used for a person who loves and admires someone or something very much, almost as if it were holy.
explain: Look at this sentence: «Picture a cold morning when you stand by a sunny window to warm up: ring-tailed lemurs do just that, sitting with arms spread wide like little sun worshippers.» The lemurs are not praying. The word is playful, and it means they love the sun and are soaking it up.
fact: A worshipper is a person who worships, such as someone who prays to God or a god.
fact: Worshippers often pray in places like churches, mosques, synagogues and temples.
fact: A sun worshipper is a playful name for someone who loves lying in the sun.
fact: Hero worship means admiring someone so much that it is almost like worship.
fact: In American English the word is spelled worshiper, with one p.
exercise: What is a worshipper in a church? | A person who sells candles at the door | A bell that rings on Sunday | *A person who prays to God or a god | A person who cleans the pews
exercise: Jayden says, «I am a sun worshipper» when he lies on the beach. What does he mean? | *He loves the sun very much | He prays to the sun in a temple | He never goes outside | He sells sunscreen on the beach
exercise: Where might worshippers go to pray together? | A swimming pool | A library | A football stadium | *A church
test: What does hero worship mean? | *Admiring someone so much it is almost like worship | Being very tall | Carrying a very heavy load | Fighting heroes in a story
test: Which is the American spelling of worshipper? | Worshyper | Worshipar | *Worshiper | Worshipper
exam: Which sentence uses worshipper in its religious sense? | Hero worship made him famous at school | The sun worshippers lay on the beach all day | *Worshippers sang and prayed together in the temple | The fans at the concert were worshippers of the band
